.TH AMIX-SADM-MIGRATE 1M "October 2026" "apkg 0.3.4" "Amix System Administration"
.SH NAME
amix-sadm-migrate \- prepare the stock package database for apkg
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B amix-sadm-migrate
[
.B \-n
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B amix-sadm-migrate
brings the package database of a stock Amix 2.1 system,
.BR /var/sadm ,
into the shape
.BR apkg (1)
and the package tools expect.  Run it once as root after installing the
APKG package; running it again changes nothing and says so.  It:
.TP 4
1.
copies
.B /var/sadm/install/contents
to
.B contents.pre-migrate
once, before any other change;
.TP
2.
adds
.B VERSION=2.1
to every
.BI /var/sadm/pkg/ pkg /pkginfo
that has no
.B VERSION=
line (the factory packages have none, so apkg could not compare them);
.TP
3.
creates every missing
.BI /var/sadm/pkg/ pkg /install
directory;
.TP
4.
sets the mode of
.B /var/sadm/install/contents
to 644 (the factory ships it writable by everyone);
.TP
5.
prints a summary of what it did.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-n
Dry run: print what would be done and change nothing.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SADM_ROOT
a directory prefixed to
.BR /var/sadm ,
for working on a tree other than the running system's
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
on success, also when there was nothing to do;
.B 1
on a usage error, when
.B /var/sadm
is missing, or when the backup fails (then nothing was changed).
.SH FILES
.PD 0
.TP 36
.B /var/sadm/install/contents
the installed-software database
.TP
.B /var/sadm/install/contents.pre-migrate
the copy made before the first change
.TP
.BI /var/sadm/pkg/ pkg /pkginfo
each installed package's parameters
.PD
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR apkg (1),
.BR contents-fsck (1M),
.BR contents (5)
